sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-glue-16> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-16--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-16--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on levin-2023-glue-16: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.45" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.448"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.58"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Cell number, cell size and tubule diameter are standard variables, and the classic paper reports the compensation down to a single curved cell. Those measurements are not in any open repository, so a check means recovering mid-century plates rather than running a deposited table. The anatomical pattern can be scrutinized from that literature; the further claim that different molecular pathways are recruited to meet a goal is not in those plates." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: In polyploid versus diploid newt embryos, count cells per pronephric-tubule cross-section, measure cell cross-sectional area, and measure lumen diameter, including the extreme in which one cell forms the wall. Matched diameter with fewer, larger cells would support size compensation; diameter scaling in proportion to cell size, or no single-cell tubules, would refute that part. Calling the match a switch among molecular mechanisms, or an anatomical goal, needs a separate assay the anatomy does not contain." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "The counts and drawings are in a 1945 journal article and later retellings, not a downloadable table or image stack.", "Cell size was changed by ploidy, which also changes nuclear content, so mechanism switching is not isolated.", "The sample is newt pronephric tubules, not kidney tubules in general." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-16--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of levin-2023-glue-16 by Grok 4.7: 0.74" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.74"^^xsd:double ;
